WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.989
(light liquid pouring)

00:00:02.989 --> 00:00:04.200
(gentle sipping)

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.090
- [Narrator] For morning
coffee to afternoon tea,

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.820
caffeine is so thoroughly
entrenched in our daily routines

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.400
and has become the worlds most widely used

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.223
psychoactive substance.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.330
Caffeine is a chemical compound

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.290
that stimulate the central nervous system.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.520
It accomplishes this by attaching itself

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.240
to adenosine receptors in the brain.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.210
In doing so, it blocks
adenosine molecules,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.310
which are responsible for slowing down

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.520
the central nervous
system before we sleep.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.610
The result?

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.310
Adenosine cannot regulate
and neurons start firing.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.790
This results in a person's reduced fatigue

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:47.000
and increased alertness
and cognitive performance.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.963
Side effects many seek
by consuming caffeine.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.120
Caffeine occurs naturally in coffee beans,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.413
tea leaves, cacao beans
and some tree nuts.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.830
People have been consuming
it for centuries.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.330
But dailY consumption
took off sporadically

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.533
at different times in different
places around the world.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.470
Coffee became popular in
the 15th and 16 centuries.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.050
But Cacao was used among early
Mesoamerican civilizations

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.500
hundreds of years earlier.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.980
Tea became popular by the 14th century

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.450
in China during the Ming dynasty,

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.313
but didn't catch on in Britain
until almost 400 years later.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.540
Today, caffeine can be
found nearly everywhere

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.070
and more and more
caffeine-infused products

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.903
are hitting the shelves everyday.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.740
In the United States,
nearly 90% of the population

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.620
has at least one caffeinated
beverage everyday.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.700
Up to 400 milligrams of caffeine
per day or about four cups

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.140
of coffee is considered safe for an adult.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:54.800
Too much caffeine for any one
person can cause side effects,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.123
such as migraines, insomnia,
nervousness and muscle tremors.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.990
One tablespoon of pure caffeine equivalent

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.880
to drinking 75 cups of coffee at once

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.053
can have lethal consequences.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.200
Due to this risk of
caffeine overdoses, in 2018,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.380
the United States Food and
Drug Administration banned

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.850
the bulk sale of products containing pure

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.913
or highly concentrated caffeine.

00:02:21.781 --> 00:02:24.740
While caffeine may provide great benefits,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.260
such as increased focus,
alertness and energy,

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.090
it comes with considerable risks

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.083
just like any other substance.

